// Roles, as far as the compiler reads them today: a world's own verbs
// played for with `permit` and `do`, an optional tool read under
// `bound`, a value tool narrowed with `from`, two kinds playing one role
// and composing, a play left out with `without`, and the actor's own part.
world roles: sprout.World {
  contains actors
  visitors are Visitor
  visitors arrive at roles
}

// The one acting plays its part too: a full pair of hands pulls nothing.
kind Visitor: sprout.Actor {
  as actor for pull {
    permit { if (self.count >= self.get(:capacity)) { refuse "Your hands are full." } }
  }
}

verb pull { role target  "pull [target]"  "yank [target]" }

// An open tool, which `"unlock [target]"` leaves out, so it is optional.
verb unlock {
  role target: Lockable
  role tool
  "unlock [target] with [tool]"
  "use [tool] on [target]"
  "unlock [target]"
}

object lever: Lever in roles
object door: Warded in roles
object gate: Rusted in roles
object key: Key in roles
object guard: Guard in roles
